Done. The package is complete and verified with 34 offline logic checks (rclpy stubbed, since ROS runs in Docker here).

## What was built — all under `ros2_stack/`

**Package** `ros2_stack/src/mower_control/` — `package.xml`, `setup.py`, `resource/`, and three nodes:

- **`cmd_vel_slew.py`** — sub `/cmd_vel_raw` → pub `/cmd_vel` (both `TwistStamped`). Fixed-rate loop slews `linear.x`/`angular.z` by `max_linear_accel` (0.5 m/s²) / `max_angular_accel` (1.0 rad/s²); other components pass through. Every published command is echoed to the log at full float precision (the MowgliNext `/cmd_vel_applied` idea as a log line). Watchdog: `cmd_timeout` 0.5 s → immediate exact zero (not slewed), held until a fresh command arrives, then slews up from zero.
- **`slip_detector.py`** — sub `/cmd_vel` plus measured twist: auto-detects `/wheel_vel` (`TwistStamped`, preferred) or falls back to `/odom` (`Odometry`) after `discovery_timeout`. Latches `/dig_stall` (`Bool`, `transient_local`) + WARN log when `|measured − commanded| > slip_threshold` (0.3) holds continuously for `slip_window` (2.0 s) on either axis; any good sample restarts the window. RTK gate via `/fix_status` from `um960_gps_driver` (substring `RTK_FIXED`, which covers both GGA quality 4 and Unicore posType 17), disableable with `require_rtk_fixed`.
- **`imu_cal.py`** — sub `/imu/data`, collects windows of `min_samples` (100), keeps only plausible ones (|accel|≈g within 0.5, non-zero but small gyro variance, |gyro bias| ≤ 0.2 rad/s — MowgliNext rules), averages gyro/accel biases, writes `~/mower_control/imu_calibration.yaml` atomically with a version header, validates any existing file on load (rejects all-zero / oversized biases), publishes `/bias_status` (`String`, `transient_local`).

**Docs** `ros2_stack/docs/control.md` — data-flow diagram, per-node topic/param tables, MowgliNext lineage (§4.3 items 7–9), run instructions, and the inter-package dependency map.

## Two things to flag

1. **`package.xml` adds `sensor_msgs`** beyond your listed deps — `imu_cal` can't subscribe to `/imu/data` (`sensor_msgs/Imu`) without it. Also added `python3-yaml` as an exec_depend.
2. **The `/fix-gated?` question** — I implemented it against the `um960_gps_driver`'s `/fix_status` string (no `mower_interfaces/GnssStatus` exists yet), behind the `require_rtk_fixed` param. When `GnssStatus` lands, that's a drop-in replacement for the substring check.

Not done (follow-ups): wiring the three nodes into `bringup.launch.py`, and a `colcon build` smoke test in the Docker image.
